1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,071
AI can help build software quickly.

2
00:00:03,071 --> 00:00:05,214
The release question is different:

3
00:00:05,214 --> 00:00:09,500
did this exact change earn evidence and an
accountable decision?

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,500
AgentProof runs deterministic collectors
without secrets and

5
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,929
binds the result to the pull-request head SHA.

6
00:00:20,929 --> 00:00:23,929
Read-only specialist sessions add context for
tests,

7
00:00:23,929 --> 00:00:26,929
security, and policy, but they remain
advisory.

8
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,929
The assembler rejects mixed repositories,
policies, or SHAs.

9
00:00:34,929 --> 00:00:38,786
The board helps people coordinate, but it is
mutable.

10
00:00:38,786 --> 00:00:43,929
The GitHub check, artifact, comments, reviews,
and commit remain the authoritative record.

11
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,357
A release manager may accept only a
policy-eligible finding,

12
00:00:55,357 --> 00:00:58,357
with a specific reason and an expiry.

13
00:00:58,357 --> 00:01:03,929
This is not an approval, and it does not
excuse the non-exceptionable failures.

14
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:11,643
The preferred path is remediation.

15
00:01:11,643 --> 00:01:15,929
The dependency is upgraded and the
authorization test is restored.

16
00:01:15,929 --> 00:01:18,929
The push creates a new head SHA,

17
00:01:18,929 --> 00:01:22,357
so this is now a new release decision.

18
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:38,643
The old exception, evidence, and approval
cannot travel across a commit change.

19
00:01:38,643 --> 00:01:42,929
AgentProof fails closed until the new revision
earns fresh evidence.

20
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:56,214
Fresh collectors and fresh specialist notes
now describe the remediated commit.

21
00:01:56,214 --> 00:02:00,071
Any remaining exception is recorded again
against this SHA,

22
00:02:00,071 --> 00:02:02,643
never copied from the previous revision.

23
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:16,357
The gate turns green only when the current
evidence,

24
00:02:16,357 --> 00:02:18,929
policy, disposition, and artifact digest
agree.

25
00:02:18,929 --> 00:02:21,929
A different human still reviews the change.

26
00:02:21,929 --> 00:02:27,071
Evidence alone cannot approve, and approval
alone cannot bypass a red gate.

27
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:36,786
This is bounded evidence for one repository,
policy, and commit.

28
00:02:36,786 --> 00:02:41,500
It does not prove universal authorship, legal
compliance, or production suitability.

29
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,500
We tested the automation boundary too.

30
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:46,833
Mutation tools remained visible,

31
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:50,500
so AgentProof stopped before using them and
the trigger was disabled.

32
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:53,500
Refusing an unsafe runtime is part of the
product.
